# Response headers, served by the origin.
#
# These four used to be a Cloudflare "Security headers" Transform Rule, because
# GitHub Pages cannot set a header at all and the edge was the only place they
# could live. Cloudflare Pages can, so they move into the repository, where they
# are diffed and reviewed like everything else rather than living in a dashboard
# nobody opens.
#
# **Every value below is byte-identical to what the Transform Rule sends today**,
# read back off the live response rather than retyped from the dashboard. That is
# deliberate and it is the whole migration plan: while both exist the browser
# receives two identical policies and enforces the same thing twice, so deleting
# the rule is provably a no-op rather than a change nobody watched. Change a value
# here only after the rule is gone.
#
# Two headers are missing from this file on purpose. `Strict-Transport-Security`
# and `X-Content-Type-Options` come from the HSTS dialog under SSL/TLS, not from
# the Transform Rule, and setting them here as well would send each one twice.
# They stay where they are.
#
# Clerk needs six allowances, added when real accounts landed. Its SDK loads
# its own script from the frontend API host encoded in the publishable key
# (script-src) and makes its own XHR/fetch calls to that same host
# (connect-src) — the dev instance lives under *.clerk.accounts.dev (kept as
# a host wildcard the same way *.giphy.com already is below, so local dev
# and any future dev-instance subdomain keep working with no edit here).
# Production moved to a verified custom domain on 1 Sep 2026 — clerk.jukeff.com,
# the exact host named in the CNAME record Clerk's own Domains page issued
# (`clerk` -> frontend-api.clerk.services), not decoded out of the
# publishable key by hand; that is one CNAME under jukeff.com, not a
# subdomain of clerk.accounts.dev, so it needed its own entry rather than
# matching the existing wildcard. img-src is Clerk's own avatar CDN
# (img.clerk.com), for <UserButton/>'s profile picture. frame-src is for
# Cloudflare Turnstile, which Clerk's sign-up flow embeds as a bot check;
# without it the widget is silently blocked by `default-src 'self'` the same
# way the script itself was before this line existed, which is exactly the
# bug that sent someone here in the first place: a click that does nothing
# and no visible error unless the console is open.
#
# Two more found only once a real draft actually ran through Clerk end to
# end, both blocked by `default-src 'self'` the same silent way:
# **worker-src `blob:`** — Clerk spins up a Web Worker from a `blob:` URL
# (its own bundled script, not a third-party host), and with no worker-src
# declared the browser falls back to script-src, which does not list
# `blob:` as a scheme. **connect-src `clerk-telemetry.com`** — Clerk's own
# usage telemetry, no different in kind from the beacon host already
# allowed above; blocking it buys nothing (it carries no script to run) and
# costs a permanently red console entry on every page load.
#
# **connect-src `*.ingest.sentry.io`** (and its `us`/`de` regions) � browser
# error reports, web/src/lib/errorMonitoring.js. connect-src only, and that
# is the whole point of how it is built: the SDK is part of our own bundle,
# loaded from 'self', so no script-src host is added and nothing third-party
# ever runs in the page. A host wildcard because the DSN names a per-org
# subdomain (o<id>.ingest.us.sentry.io); CSP3 lets `*.` match more than one
# label. With no VITE_SENTRY_DSN nothing ever connects there.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://*.clerk.accounts.dev https://clerk.jukeff.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' https://sleepercdn.com https://*.giphy.com https://img.clerk.com; connect-src 'self' https://juke-draft-room.jukeff.workers.dev wss://juke-draft-room.jukeff.workers.dev https://site.api.espn.com https://*.clerk.accounts.dev https://clerk.jukeff.com https://clerk-telemetry.com https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://*.ingest.us.sentry.io https://*.ingest.de.sentry.io; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
